review.json; rawSHA256=db281bc43f4d0e781acfc8ef4b03f93794e75d6a4d62ea174b1a917832b6c326. Original request rawSHA256=14efb3eb5bd505eb0135d80fd3a358551efc6d9ad52af824c78efd836c03993b. Prior reviewer final text=/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/d9b1/lemmadeck/.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-182/tmp/batch318-8a-first-figure-review/n6/reviewer-final.txt; rawSHA256=ebf581d7a47e172d16ef46f4508cdb1df632ea92b9d918ec02b345213721db17. I read that real prior final text: all three original gates were FAIL specifically because their actual native previews were not 640 pixels wide; the prior source/native reviewer genuinely completed its source comparison and reported no observed native label collisions or edge clipping, visible faceting and uncertified exact centerlines/terminals. That reviewer performed three record_review.py invocations with exits 0/0/0 and six original/native image opens; none are my actions.\n\nFrozen inputs verified as bytes only and unchanged: source SHA256=fe34acf9d462941b26391216679569ccb33e1859c6d1f44806a7f1db759f82b6; native preview rawSHA256=46727ae23b6e51b7202f8b050cae4a9f30a719ab410e945a0b76562c69234646 (historical native dimensions 516x876); spec rawSHA256=796d7c723f94529586b4d311fcbb93e0600d64461b862f32cf108588a5a5567b; render rawSHA256=fb25be94df48b57b4d1015ff8d349e938147442849d10aa0417892c6138c4c8b; SVG rawSHA256=3f86cb5dd9bf013449182f53d8fb7cd81561587e19f3829cec70c14395351937; context SHA256=a9d05c5f8222a2e0f59be26c8a699649228e142afd0aa2f04ae7f8230148c73e; host HTML rawSHA256=960624d838d24b93864be5068664aa499fc184bd78c3ba377ef53465a2acff13. Host HTML was hash-only, never content-inspected. Source/native PNGs were hashed only, never opened or decoded here. The complete actual640 dimensions and actual_capture_measurement={\"width\":640,\"height\":1086.5,\"naturalWidth\":516,\"naturalHeight\":876,\"complete\":true} are supplied parent capture evidence, not my independent DOM/browser/capture action. This is not another cap2 render or repair.\n\nINHERITED P